# 🚀 VOIDCHAT — full setup & publish guide

## Part 0 — What you need before starting

You should already have:
- ✅ Your project folder with these 6 files: `index.html`, `styles.css`, `script.js`, `firebase.json`, `database.rules.json`, `.firebaserc`
- ✅ A **Google account** (any Gmail works)
- ✅ **Node.js** installed on your PC — check by opening Command Prompt / PowerShell and typing:
  ```bash
  node -v
  ```
  If you see something like `v18.x.x` or higher, you're good. If you see "command not found", download from https://nodejs.org/ → install the **LTS** version → restart your PC.

---

## Part 1 — Create the Firebase project

1. Go to **https://console.firebase.google.com/**
2. Sign in with your Google account.
3. Click the big **"Create a project"** card (or "Add project" if you've used Firebase before).
4. **Project name:** type something like `voidchat-school` (any name works — must be unique across all Firebase). Click **Continue**.
5. **Google Analytics:** toggle it **OFF** (you don't need it for this) → Click **Continue** → **Create project**.
6. Wait ~30 seconds for the rocket animation. Click **Continue** when it's done.

You're now in the project dashboard.

> ⚠️ **Important:** Look at the URL or the top of the page — somewhere you'll see your **Project ID** (something like `voidchat-school-a1b2c`). Write it down — you'll need it twice.

---

## Part 2 — Enable Anonymous Authentication

This lets your visitors chat **without signing up** — they just open the link and they're in.

1. In the left sidebar, click **Build** to expand it.
2. Click **Authentication**.
3. Click the big **"Get started"** button.
4. You'll see a list of sign-in methods. Click **Anonymous**.
5. Flip the **Enable** toggle ON → click **Save**.

✅ Done. Your app can now silently sign users in.

---

## Part 3 — Create the Realtime Database

This is where messages, users, and presence data are stored.

1. In the left sidebar (still under **Build**), click **Realtime Database**.
   - ⚠️ Make sure it's **Realtime Database**, NOT "Firestore Database". They are different products.
2. Click **"Create Database"**.
3. **Location:** pick the closest one to you (e.g. `europe-west1` for Europe, `us-central1` for US). Click **Next**.
4. **Security rules:** select **"Start in locked mode"** (we'll deploy proper rules in Part 7). Click **Enable**.
5. Once it loads, you'll see an empty database with a URL at the top like:
   ```
   https://voidchat-school-a1b2c-default-rtdb.europe-west1.firebasedatabase.app/
   ```
   👉 **Copy this URL** — you'll paste it in Part 5.

---

## Part 4 — Register your web app & get the config

Firebase needs to know your website exists.

1. At the top of the page, click the **gear icon** ⚙️ next to "Project Overview" → click **Project settings**.
2. Scroll down to **"Your apps"**.
3. Click the **`</>`** (web) icon — this means "I'm building a web app".
4. **App nickname:** type `voidchat` (any name) → leave "Firebase Hosting" checkbox **unchecked** for now (we'll do hosting via the command line) → click **Register app**.
5. Firebase shows you a code snippet with a `firebaseConfig = { ... }` object. It looks like this:
   ```js
   const firebaseConfig = {
     apiKey: "AIzaSyC9_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
     authDomain: "voidchat-school-a1b2c.firebaseapp.com",
     databaseURL: "https://voidchat-school-a1b2c-default-rtdb.europe-west1.firebasedatabase.app",
     projectId: "voidchat-school-a1b2c",
     storageBucket: "voidchat-school-a1b2c.appspot.com",
     messagingSenderId: "123456789012",
     appId: "1:123456789012:web:abc123def456"
   };
   ```
6. **Copy this whole block somewhere safe** (Notepad is fine). Don't worry about hiding the apiKey — for Firebase web apps it's **not secret**; security comes from the rules we'll deploy.
7. Click **"Continue to console"**.

> 🔍 **Note:** if you don't see `databaseURL` in the snippet, manually add it using the URL you copied in Part 3.

