## Part 8 — Deploy security rules (CRITICAL!)

Before going live, you must publish the database rules. Right now your DB is in "locked mode" — even *your own* app can't write to it.

In the same terminal (still inside your project folder), run:
```bash
firebase deploy --only database
```

Output ends with:
```
✔ Deploy complete!
```

Now go back to Firebase Console → **Realtime Database** → click the **Rules** tab. You should see the long ruleset starting with `"publicMessages"`. ✅

---

## Part 9 — Publish (deploy hosting) 🚀

The big moment. From your terminal:

```bash
firebase deploy
```

This uploads everything AND your rules in one go. After 30 seconds you'll see:

```
✔ Deploy complete!

Project Console: https://console.firebase.google.com/project/voidchat-school-a1b2c
Hosting URL:     https://voidchat-school-a1b2c.web.app
```

🎉 **That Hosting URL is your public website.** Open it in your browser. Send it to friends. They can chat with you in real time.

Your site is also automatically available at:
- `https://voidchat-school-a1b2c.web.app`
- `https://voidchat-school-a1b2c.firebaseapp.com`

(Both work, both are free, both have HTTPS.)

---

## Part 10 — Updating the site later

Any time you change `index.html`, `styles.css`, or `script.js`:

```bash
firebase deploy --only hosting
```

That's it. Changes go live in ~10 seconds.

If you change `database.rules.json`:
```bash
firebase deploy --only database
```

Or both at once:
```bash
firebase deploy
```

