## 🆘 Troubleshooting cheat sheet

| Symptom | Cause / Fix |
|---|---|
| Stays "OFFLINE", browser console shows `auth/configuration-not-found` | Anonymous Auth not enabled → redo **Part 2** |
| Stays "OFFLINE", console shows `permission_denied` | Database rules not deployed → run `firebase deploy --only database` (Part 8) |
| Stays "OFFLINE", console shows `Invalid API key` | Wrong `apiKey` in `firebaseConfig` → recopy from **Part 4** |
| Messages don't appear for the other tab | Your `databaseURL` is wrong or missing — recheck Part 5. Both tabs must point to the same URL. |
| `firebase: command not found` after install | Close & reopen your terminal. On Windows, sometimes you need to add npm's global folder to PATH. |
| `Error: Failed to authenticate` on deploy | Run `firebase logout` then `firebase login` again. |
| `Error: HTTP Error 403, The caller does not have permission` | You're logged into the wrong Google account in the CLI. Run `firebase logout` → `firebase login` and pick the right one. |
| Want to deploy to a different project | `firebase use --add` → pick another project from the list |

